  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  @  TTestW
  @  Two independent samples, unequal variances (Welch t test).
  @  Author & design           : Jean Wilson
  @  Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @  Arguments may be given loose or bundled in a list of 6; that list is
  @  what LastArguments reports, and its length is checked before use.
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  IF DUP TypeName "list" == THEN IF DUP Size 6 ≠ THEN "TTestW: needs 6 arguments" DoError END Explode Drop END
  → n1v x1v s1v n2v x2v s2v « n1v 0 + x1v 0 + s1v 0 + n2v 0 + x2v 0 + s2v 0 + → n1 xb1 sd1 n2 xb2 sd2 « 'sd1^2/n1' →Num 'sd2^2/n2' →Num → va vb « '(xb1-xb2)/√(va+vb)' →Num '(va+vb)^2/(va^2/(n1-1)+vb^2/(n2-1))' →Num → tv dfv « tv "t" →Tag dfv "df" →Tag dfv 'ABS(tv)' →Num UTPT 2 * "p" →Tag n1v x1v s1v n2v x2v s2v 6 →List Drop » » » »
